1
00:00:01,199 --> 00:00:06,482
My name is Ruth Masih. I'm a nurse in Lucknow. And that day I

2
00:00:06,482 --> 00:00:12,890
learned that a child's marks and a child's worth are two different things.

3
00:00:14,039 --> 00:00:17,783
That morning I put the tea on like always. But

4
00:00:17,783 --> 00:00:22,829
my hands were shaking. The NEET results were coming out today.

5
00:00:23,379 --> 00:00:28,602
My son Aman, seventeen. Two years of coaching, six in

6
00:00:28,602 --> 00:00:34,219
the morning to ten at night. This was his second attempt.

7
00:00:35,369 --> 00:00:46,060
Slips of paper covered his wall. Physics formulas, chemistry lists, and one slip that said, Dr. Aman Masih.

8
00:00:46,609 --> 00:00:51,740
He didn't write that slip. His father did.

9
00:00:52,890 --> 00:00:58,800
Daniel is a good man. He's a bank clerk. But his dream was for

10
00:00:58,800 --> 00:01:05,950
someone from our home to become a doctor. His father couldn't. He couldn't.

11
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:17,629
And then the relatives. Every wedding, every festival, the same question. What happened with Aman? Auntie's daughter is at AIIMS.

12
00:01:18,780 --> 00:01:29,599
The result came at eleven. I heard no sound from his room. No scream, no crying. Just silence.

13
00:01:30,150 --> 00:01:35,319
Then I heard the door close. And the latch.

14
00:01:36,469 --> 00:01:43,750
I called out. Aman, beta, open the door. No answer.

15
00:01:44,299 --> 00:01:54,090
His phone was off. I'm a nurse. I've seen a lot in the hospital. In that moment my heart sank.

16
00:01:55,239 --> 00:02:02,807
I sat right there on the floor, my back against the door. I didn't

17
00:02:02,807 --> 00:02:10,719
pray loudly. I just said softly, Lord, hold my son. I can't hold him.

18
00:02:11,270 --> 00:02:15,289
And then I remembered the verse my mother used to say to me.

19
00:02:16,439 --> 00:02:27,020
I will praise thee; for I am fearfully and wonderfully made. Psalm 139:14.

20
00:02:28,169 --> 00:02:34,822
I said through the door, Aman, you know, I failed too. The nursing entrance,

21
00:02:34,822 --> 00:02:42,000
the first time. Your grandfather didn't hand out sweets to the whole neighborhood.

22
00:02:42,550 --> 00:02:52,439
I cried for three days. Then my mother said, Ruth, God made you with His hands, not with numbers.

23
00:02:52,990 --> 00:02:58,319
No sound came from inside. But I didn't stop talking.

24
00:02:59,469 --> 00:03:09,800
Then I opened the app my sister put on my phone. Community Covenant. It has a box: How are you?

25
00:03:10,349 --> 00:03:20,389
I wrote, my son is broken. The door is shut. I don't know what to say. I'm scared.

26
00:03:21,539 --> 00:03:28,774
Ruth, you are not alone. He doesn't need answers right now, he needs your

27
00:03:28,774 --> 00:03:35,909
presence. Just stay there. Tell him his worth isn't decided by a result.

28
00:03:36,460 --> 00:03:47,430
And if you feel he's in danger, call for help now. In India, Tele-MANAS, 14416, is open day and night.

29
00:03:48,580 --> 00:03:55,570
So I said exactly that. Aman, I don't need a doctor. I

30
00:03:55,570 --> 00:04:02,689
need my son. Marks can change. You can't. You are mine.

31
00:04:03,840 --> 00:04:14,229
After a while the latch opened. His eyes were swollen. All he said was, Mummy, what will Papa say?

32
00:04:14,780 --> 00:04:20,850
I ruined everything, Mummy. Two years. All of Papa's money.

33
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:31,040
I held him. I didn't say anything. Sometimes a mother's job isn't to speak, just to hold on.

34
00:04:32,189 --> 00:04:39,399
In the evening Daniel came home. I was afraid. But he had a box of jalebis in his hand.

35
00:04:39,949 --> 00:04:46,081
Aman, come here. I sat at the bank today and thought a lot. Your

36
00:04:46,081 --> 00:04:52,980
grandfather put his dream on me too. I repeated the same mistake on you.

37
00:04:53,529 --> 00:04:59,069
Forgive me, son. You are my son, not my dream.

38
00:05:00,220 --> 00:05:07,093
That night we didn't talk about the result. We ate jalebis. Our daughter Neha told

39
00:05:07,093 --> 00:05:13,379
a silly joke from school, and Aman laughed for the first time in two years.

40
00:05:14,529 --> 00:05:21,470
Then we prayed together. Daniel read the verse that's now on our fridge.

41
00:05:22,019 --> 00:05:28,415
For I know the thoughts that I think toward you, saith

42
00:05:28,415 --> 00:05:35,639
the Lord, thoughts of peace, and not of evil. Jeremiah 29:11.

43
00:05:36,790 --> 00:05:42,328
A few weeks later Aman decided for himself. He said, Mummy,

44
00:05:42,328 --> 00:05:46,740
I want to help people, but I need my peace too.

45
00:05:47,290 --> 00:05:56,319
Now he's studying physiotherapy. Sometimes he comes to my hospital. The elderly patients love him.

46
00:05:57,470 --> 00:06:03,540
I'm telling you this because every year lakhs of children go through this same

47
00:06:03,540 --> 00:06:09,610
day. And every year lakhs of parents have just one moment, the first sentence.

48
00:06:10,160 --> 00:06:17,240
That first sentence decides whether the child hears, I'm a failure, or hears, you are mine.

49
00:06:18,389 --> 00:06:28,589
Whatsoever ye do, do it heartily, as to the Lord, and not unto men. Colossians 3:23.

50
00:06:29,139 --> 00:06:36,351
If your child came home with a result today, what would you say to them first?

51
00:06:36,351 --> 00:06:43,470
Write it in the comments. And send this video to a parent who needs it today.

52
00:06:46,223 --> 00:06:50,388
If a day like this comes to your home too, don't stay alone.

53
00:06:50,988 --> 00:06:56,010
Open the Community Covenant app. The link is in the description below.

54
00:06:56,610 --> 00:07:04,221
Tap "Ask for Help" and write how you are. Write what's in your heart.

55
00:07:04,821 --> 00:07:11,495
That same day someone from our team will answer you and pray

56
00:07:11,495 --> 00:07:17,613
for you. And tap "Listen" to hear God's Word for today.

57
00:07:18,213 --> 00:07:27,268
It's free. And if anyone is in danger, call Tele-MANAS at 14416 right now.
